id: 1929-08-23-riots-in-palestine-over-access
when: 1929-08-23
where: [jerusalem]  # TODO(migration): matched from the title; verify
actors: [uk]  # auto-tagged from text: uk
---
## Riots in Palestine over access to the Western Wall in Jerusalem.

116 Arabs and 133 Jews are killed. Hebron massacre (Aug 24), where a mob of Palestinians kills 68 Jews. According to some historians, the uprising was also triggered by the refusal of Zionist leaders to accept British offers of shared representation in Palestine which was accepted by the Arab leadership.[1] According to other historians, the riots were caused by the mufti trying to strengthen his position by rousing fears of a Jewish takeover of the Temple Mount.[2] Scholars have also pointed to the transfer of land to the Jewish National Fund, which, along with rising concerns over land sales and immigration, contributed to socioeconomic anxieties that helped fuel the outbreak.

---
id: 1936-04-20-arab-revolt
